====================================

Everything not listed here is the Tango authors' own code under the MIT licence in LICENSE (each
file's SPDX header says so).


TEMLIB ascal (AVALON SCALER)
----------------------------
Files:  ascal.vhd
        ascal_ghdl/ascal_fixed.v   (GHDL's machine translation of ascal.vhd into a Verilog netlist;
                                    ascal_ghdl/gen.sh regenerates it; same terms as ascal.vhd)
        ascal_ghdl/ascal_poly_bram.patch   (the Tango authors' modification of ascal.vhd, 2026-10-03: its
                                    polyphase coefficient memories as synchronous-read RAMs, so they become block
                                    RAM; ascal.vhd itself is unchanged.  Same terms as ascal.vhd)
        ascal_ghdl/ascal_fixed8.v  (GHDL's translation of ascal.vhd with that patch, FRAC 8: the netlist of the
                                    TANGO_VIDEO_PROC builds; ascal_ghdl/gen.sh 8 regenerates it; same terms)
        ascal_ghdl/ascal_fixed_ddr3.v, ascal_ghdl/ascal_fixed8_ddr3.v   (the same two translations with the
                                    Avalon side of the DDR3 scaler port: the TANGO_VIDEO_DDR3 builds;
                                    ascal_ghdl/gen.sh 4d / 8d regenerate them; same terms)

Source: ascal.vhd is byte-identical to sys/ascal.vhd of MiSTer-devel/Genesis_MiSTer at commit
        adc0c42cfb1fa5d484cc8566767f7d68982bc44a ("Release 20230224"), i.e. TEMLIB's scaler as
        carried and extended by the MiSTer project.  That repository as a whole is GPL-3.0; this
        file states its own terms, its header verbatim:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- AVALON SCALER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- TEMLIB 2018 - 2020
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- This code can be freely distributed and used for any purpose, but, if you
-- find any bug, or want to suggest an enhancement, you ought to send a mail
-- to info@temlib.org.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Modified: the TEMLIB terms allow it ("freely distributed and used for any purpose").  The modification is the
patch alone, applied by gen.sh 8 to a copy; its header says what it changes and why (the reads one clock ahead
with the addresses the old reads used one clock later, the writes one statement per memory: the same picture on
every clock while no coefficient is written).  As the header asks, an enhancement may be sent to info@temlib.org.

The wrapper around it (ascal_wrap.v, ascal_wrap_sim.v, ascal_ghdl/ascal_fixed.vhd, ascal_fixed8.vhd,
ascal_fixed_ddr3.vhd, ascal_fixed8_ddr3.vhd, ascal_ghdl/ascal_shim.v, ascal_shim8.v, ascal_shim_ddr3.v,
ascal_shim8_ddr3.v, ascal_ghdl/gen.sh) is the Tango authors' own code (MIT).


